    "question": "5: collapsed versus too_large, and other ways to read a withheld diff",
    "source": "gitlab-org/gitlab MR 252015, compared through /repository/compare from base_sha to head_sha",
    "finding": "The compare endpoint marks large files collapsed true with too_large false and diff '' (even locale/de/gitlab.po, which /diffs sent in full), so collapsed carries no diff either. GET /merge_requests/:iid/raw_diffs returned the whole MR as one 3,898,803-byte text/plain unified diff that does include the too_large files (fr/gitlab.po: 499 hunks), but it has no per-file filter and grows with the whole MR, so it is not a bounded per-file source.",
